# Local multi-arch image builds

On this amd64 workstation, build milk-ddp container images with **buildah**, not
`podman build --platform` / qemu-user binfmt. Host binfmt for aarch64 is broken
here (`Exec format error`); do not waste time on qemu workarounds.

## Commands

Native amd64 Alpine (preferred local smoke image):

```bash
buildah bud -f Dockerfile.alpine \
  -t localhost/milk-ddp:dev \
  -t localhost/milk-ddp:test-audio-gain \
  .
```

Cross / multi-arch with buildah (when an arm64 image is required locally):

```bash
buildah bud --arch arm64 --os linux -f Dockerfile.alpine \
  -t localhost/milk-ddp:dev-arm64 \
  .
```

Manifest list (optional):

```bash
buildah manifest create localhost/milk-ddp:dev
buildah manifest add localhost/milk-ddp:dev localhost/milk-ddp:dev
buildah manifest add --arch arm64 localhost/milk-ddp:dev localhost/milk-ddp:dev-arm64
```

## Ship to NanoPi R3S (aarch64)

Prefer `podman image scp` after a local arm64 buildah image exists:

```bash
podman image scp localhost/milk-ddp:dev-arm64 stephen@nanopi-r3s.lan::
```

Or save/load into the **rootful** store used by `sudo podman kube play`:

```bash
podman save localhost/milk-ddp:dev-arm64 | ssh stephen@nanopi-r3s.lan 'sudo podman load'
```

Do not assume rootless and rootful image stores are shared on the NanoPi.
